     4→/**
     5→ * SplitViewComponent
     6→ *
     7→ * Responsive split-view layout supporting:
     8→ * - Desktop (>=1024px): Side-by-side with draggable divider
     9→ * - Tablet (768px-1023px): Tabbed layout
    10→ * - Mobile (<768px): Single panel with external toggle
    11→ *
    12→ * CRITICAL: Uses a SINGLE ng-content per slot (Angular only projects once).
    13→ * Responsive behavior is achieved via CSS media queries + data-attributes,
    14→ * NOT by duplicating ng-content in separate template branches.
    15→ */
    16→@Component({
    17→  selector: 'app-split-view',
    18→  standalone: true,
    19→  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
    20→  imports: [CommonModule],
    21→  template: `
    22→    <!-- Tablet/Mobile tab bar (hidden on desktop) -->
    23→    <div class="lg:hidden border-b border-gray-200 flex flex-shrink-0 bg-white" role="tablist">
